00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:05,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:05,877 --> 00:00:07,879
What are you guys doing? Ryunosuke!

2
00:00:07,946 --> 00:00:08,780
What is it?

3
00:00:09,347 --> 00:00:10,448
What the hell are you up to?!

4
00:00:11,316 --> 00:00:12,584
Don't misunderstand!

5
00:00:13,151 --> 00:00:14,352
What do you mean?

6
00:00:14,919 --> 00:00:16,354
I fell for him.

7
00:00:16,955 --> 00:00:17,789
I fell for Ryu-chan.

8
00:00:19,057 --> 00:00:19,891
Ryu-chan?

9
00:00:21,526 --> 00:00:23,862
Are you both dating?

10
00:00:23,928 --> 00:00:25,096
-Yes.
-No.

11
00:00:25,163 --> 00:00:26,064
What?

12
00:00:26,131 --> 00:00:28,867
No way! We are dating, aren't we?

13
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:30,702
No, I wouldn't say we're there yet.

14
00:00:30,768 --> 00:00:32,537
We even went on three dates!

15
00:00:32,604 --> 00:00:36,241
That was because we happened
to want to see the same movie.

16
00:00:36,307 --> 00:00:39,344
We text every day!
"Good morning" and "Good night."

17
00:00:39,911 --> 00:00:41,679
Friends do that too.

18
00:00:41,746 --> 00:00:44,082
Wait a second, you two.

19
00:00:44,949 --> 00:00:45,917
What?

20
00:00:46,985 --> 00:00:49,988
This comes down to
what "dating" actually consists of.

21
00:00:50,522 --> 00:00:54,359
For high schoolers, declaring
that you're dating makes it so,

22
00:00:54,425 --> 00:00:56,794
but for adults, you need to have
at least kissed, right?

23
00:00:56,861 --> 00:00:59,430
Mr. Onizuka, we don't need
to define it right now.

24
00:00:59,497 --> 00:01:00,832
Oh, sorry.

25
00:01:00,899 --> 00:01:03,001
Ryu-chan, how do you feel about me?

26
00:01:03,735 --> 00:01:04,569
What?

27
00:01:04,636 --> 00:01:08,673
I was thinking of asking you to be
my boyfriend on our next date.

28
00:01:10,108 --> 00:01:11,109
That is…

29
00:01:11,676 --> 00:01:15,380
Ms. Kotone, right now we need
to think about how to resolve this.

30
00:01:15,446 --> 00:01:17,949
What? Can't things just stay
the way they were?

31
00:01:18,016 --> 00:01:19,517
Well…

32
00:01:20,084 --> 00:01:20,952
Listen,

33
00:01:21,019 --> 00:01:24,689
you're both good people, so I'd like
to let you do as you please, but…

34
00:01:24,756 --> 00:01:27,659
I don't mind if everyone finds out.

35
00:01:27,725 --> 00:01:29,093
Because I love Ryu-chan.

36
00:01:29,761 --> 00:01:31,129
Don't just say that.

37
00:01:31,196 --> 00:01:33,331
If that happens,
you'll be the most impacted.

38
00:01:33,398 --> 00:01:36,034
I don't care.
As long as I can be with you.

39
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:38,536
Come now, let's calm down, Kotone.

40
00:01:38,603 --> 00:01:40,305
For now, let's do this…

41
00:01:41,439 --> 00:01:42,273
I mean…

42
00:01:43,341 --> 00:01:45,910
Let's do as Ms. Kashiwabara says.

43
00:01:45,977 --> 00:01:48,046
No, don't pass it over to me.

44
00:01:48,846 --> 00:01:50,315
Please!

45
00:01:50,381 --> 00:01:55,019
You noticed the two of them before I did,
and besides, I'm bad with romantic stuff.

46
00:01:55,086 --> 00:01:56,421
I've never been popular.

47
00:01:56,487 --> 00:01:58,156
Even if you say that…

48
00:01:58,223 --> 00:01:59,791
Where is the meeting room?

49
00:02:00,358 --> 00:02:03,494
For now, I think it's better
if you two don't talk at school.

50
00:02:03,561 --> 00:02:05,129
You never know who's watching.

51
00:02:06,097 --> 00:02:08,366
Oh, that's a good idea. Okay?

52
00:02:09,267 --> 00:02:13,271
You mustn't tell anyone about this.

53
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:20,511
What should we do?

54
00:02:20,578 --> 00:02:22,880
We can't just leave it like this forever.

55
00:02:23,414 --> 00:02:26,951
I'm at a loss. It's my first time
dealing with a problem like this.

56
00:02:29,721 --> 00:02:30,888
Excuse me.

57
00:02:35,193 --> 00:02:36,194
Is something wrong?

58
00:02:36,261 --> 00:02:37,095
No…

59
00:02:37,161 --> 00:02:40,832
My wife, who went back to her parents,
hasn't sent me any texts lately.

60
00:02:40,898 --> 00:02:42,634
What do you think I should do?

61
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:44,836
Don't dump your family issues on me too.

62
00:02:44,902 --> 00:02:46,070
Don't say that.

63
00:02:46,738 --> 00:02:48,573
As a woman,
please give me some good advice.

64
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:49,607
Give me a break.

65
00:02:49,674 --> 00:02:51,009
Excuse me.

66
00:02:55,813 --> 00:02:57,348
To my dearest wife.

67
00:02:57,415 --> 00:03:00,251
Are things still the same with you?

68
00:03:00,318 --> 00:03:02,954
Everyone's here.

69
00:03:03,021 --> 00:03:04,922
Let's make today a good day too.

70
00:03:05,490 --> 00:03:09,661
On my side, the terrible posts
slandering me have stopped,

71
00:03:09,727 --> 00:03:14,966
and everyone in the class
is looking up at me from their tablets.

72
00:03:15,033 --> 00:03:17,935
Our class is the only one
that hasn't decided what to do

73
00:03:18,002 --> 00:03:19,437
for the culture festival.

74
00:03:19,504 --> 00:03:22,040
It's about time we decided.

75
00:03:22,106 --> 00:03:23,508
What should we do?

76
00:03:23,574 --> 00:03:25,276
-What do you want to do?
-What?

77
00:03:25,343 --> 00:03:28,780
I think we should serve chocolate bananas…

78
00:03:35,253 --> 00:03:36,387
Mr. Onizuka, may I?

79
00:03:36,454 --> 00:03:37,422
What's up, Yuu?

80
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:42,060
Actually, I have an announcement
for everyone.

81
00:03:43,428 --> 00:03:48,232
Seishin is the newest member
of our Drill Team!

82
00:03:48,299 --> 00:03:49,567
Really?

83
00:03:49,634 --> 00:03:52,570
Actually, I always thought
what you were doing looked fun.

84
00:03:52,637 --> 00:03:55,907
We have now finally gathered five members.

85
00:03:55,973 --> 00:04:00,011
We're going to try to get recognized
as a real team by the school!

86
00:04:01,012 --> 00:04:03,648
I'm still the club president.
Keep that in mind!

87
00:04:03,715 --> 00:04:05,950
All right, good luck then!

88
00:04:06,017 --> 00:04:07,785
Yeah!

89
00:04:12,090 --> 00:04:13,391
Do your best.

90
00:04:14,092 --> 00:04:18,663
And I thought my happy ending
had finally come, but…

91
00:05:46,717 --> 00:05:48,252
-Mr. Onizuka.
-What is it?

92
00:05:49,153 --> 00:05:52,890
I think I should tell my parents,
about Ryu-chan.

93
00:05:52,957 --> 00:05:54,492
No, wait a minute!

94
00:05:54,559 --> 00:05:56,627
You promised not to tell
anyone, didn't you?

95
00:05:56,694 --> 00:05:59,230
Why can't I tell the world
about the man I love?

96
00:05:59,297 --> 00:06:00,965
Well, you know…

97
00:06:01,532 --> 00:06:03,534
You should have a talk
with Ryunosuke first.

98
00:06:03,601 --> 00:06:06,170
Even if I do that,
my feelings won't change.

99
00:06:06,237 --> 00:06:07,638
Don't say that.

100
00:06:08,639 --> 00:06:09,907
Kotone…

101
00:06:33,564 --> 00:06:36,701
Please, send me a reply.

102
00:06:36,767 --> 00:06:41,138
For my whole life,
I don't plan to love any woman

103
00:06:41,205 --> 00:06:42,607
other than you!

104
00:06:46,911 --> 00:06:50,081
Are you writing a love letter
to Ms. Fuyutsuki?

105
00:06:50,147 --> 00:06:52,416
You startled me. Why are you here?

106
00:06:52,917 --> 00:06:55,953
Can't you tell? I'm here for work.

107
00:06:57,388 --> 00:07:00,358
What's wrong, Onicchi? You look so stern.

108
00:07:00,424 --> 00:07:01,692
No, I mean…

109
00:07:01,759 --> 00:07:06,330
A problem came up with a girl in my class.

110
00:07:06,397 --> 00:07:08,332
What if that girl…

111
00:07:08,399 --> 00:07:09,433
That girl?

112
00:07:10,801 --> 00:07:13,004
Never mind, consulting you
won't do any good anyway.

113
00:07:13,070 --> 00:07:14,972
Don't say that.

114
00:07:15,039 --> 00:07:17,642
My daughter goes to this high school too.

115
00:07:17,708 --> 00:07:21,212
As a representative of the parents,
I can give you my valuable opinion.

116
00:07:24,415 --> 00:07:25,516
Don't tell anyone.

117
00:07:25,583 --> 00:07:27,985
Don't worry, my lips are sealed.

118
00:07:28,052 --> 00:07:29,220
Listen up.

119
00:07:29,287 --> 00:07:31,155
You must have met him before.

120
00:07:31,222 --> 00:07:33,991
Ryunosuke Miyazawa, my former student.

121
00:07:34,058 --> 00:07:36,327
Right, that sincere-looking young man.

122
00:07:37,395 --> 00:07:38,796
Turns out…

123
00:07:38,863 --> 00:07:43,801
He has been secretly dating
a girl in my class.

124
00:07:43,868 --> 00:07:45,836
No way? Who's the girl?

125
00:07:45,903 --> 00:07:47,071
I can't tell you that.

126
00:07:47,638 --> 00:07:49,807
Don't tell me it's Kotone Wakatsuki?

127
00:07:50,341 --> 00:07:51,943
-How do you know?
-What?

128
00:07:52,009 --> 00:07:53,010
What?

129
00:07:54,045 --> 00:07:55,212
What did you say?

130
00:07:57,982 --> 00:08:00,585
Hey, where are you going?

131
00:08:00,651 --> 00:08:03,120
I'll kill the bastard
who messed with my daughter!

132
00:08:04,455 --> 00:08:07,325
Hey, where's Ryunosuke Miyazawa?

133
00:08:07,892 --> 00:08:10,962
I might be dressed like this,
but I'm not on duty right now!

134
00:08:11,028 --> 00:08:12,129
I'm a parent!

135
00:08:12,196 --> 00:08:13,864
Hey, wait a minute!

136
00:08:13,931 --> 00:08:15,600
You were Kotone's father?

137
00:08:15,666 --> 00:08:17,001
That's why I'm so mad!

138
00:08:17,068 --> 00:08:20,137
But you don't look alike,
and your last names are different.

139
00:08:20,204 --> 00:08:22,506
I divorced Kotone's mother
a long time ago.

140
00:08:22,573 --> 00:08:24,175
Oh, I see.

141
00:08:25,409 --> 00:08:26,243
Hello!

142
00:08:28,312 --> 00:08:29,280
Ryunosuke!

143
00:08:30,414 --> 00:08:32,583
Mr. Masaru, right? Hello.

144
00:08:32,650 --> 00:08:34,318
Don't play dumb with me, asshole!

145
00:08:34,385 --> 00:08:36,520
You bastard! You laid
your hands on my daughter!

146
00:08:36,587 --> 00:08:39,523
Calm down, Masaru… I mean, Kotone's dad.

147
00:08:39,590 --> 00:08:41,359
Violence is bad!

148
00:08:41,425 --> 00:08:44,495
Onicchi, you too! What are you doing?
You're her homeroom teacher!

149
00:08:44,562 --> 00:08:46,964
Wait, what are you doing, Dad?

150
00:08:48,733 --> 00:08:50,134
Listen to me, Kotone.

151
00:08:50,201 --> 00:08:52,870
Don't be fooled by a guy like this!

152
00:08:52,937 --> 00:08:54,271
What are you talking about?

153
00:08:54,338 --> 00:08:57,008
You made Mom cry so much back then.

154
00:08:57,508 --> 00:08:59,477
What right do you have to judge others?

155
00:08:59,543 --> 00:09:01,078
So you told him already?

156
00:09:01,145 --> 00:09:04,749
I had no idea Masaru was her father.

157
00:09:05,449 --> 00:09:07,351
What on earth is going on here?

158
00:09:07,418 --> 00:09:09,286
You're being so loud.

159
00:09:09,353 --> 00:09:11,822
Is there some trouble
with the delivery company?

160
00:09:11,889 --> 00:09:13,591
It's nothing like that, you idiot.

161
00:09:13,658 --> 00:09:15,593
Long time no see, Nakamaru. Listen up!

162
00:09:15,660 --> 00:09:17,895
This Ryunosuke Miyazawa guy and my--

163
00:09:17,962 --> 00:09:20,498
It's nothing!
Just a small misunderstanding!

164
00:09:20,564 --> 00:09:23,267
You go on home.
Kotone, go back to the classroom.

165
00:09:23,334 --> 00:09:24,735
-Onicchi!
-Dad!

166
00:09:25,770 --> 00:09:28,105
I love Ryu-chan.

167
00:09:28,172 --> 00:09:29,940
I want to be with him until I die.

168
00:09:37,348 --> 00:09:38,649
Don't be stupid, Kotone.

169
00:09:38,716 --> 00:09:40,117
No matter what anyone says,

170
00:09:40,785 --> 00:09:42,386
my feelings won't change.

171
00:09:42,453 --> 00:09:46,757
How dare you make my daughter
say such things, you bastard!

172
00:09:46,824 --> 00:09:48,559
Sir! Please calm down.

173
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:53,998
Mr. Miyazawa, could you explain
what is going on here?

174
00:09:55,733 --> 00:10:01,305
I met with Ms. Kotone Wakatsuki
in private about three times.

175
00:10:01,372 --> 00:10:02,206
But…

176
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:06,343
Nothing improper ever occurred.

177
00:10:07,078 --> 00:10:08,112
So…

178
00:10:12,416 --> 00:10:13,651
I will never meet

179
00:10:16,087 --> 00:10:17,788
your daughter again.

180
00:10:17,855 --> 00:10:20,391
I'm sorry for my carelessness.

181
00:10:20,458 --> 00:10:22,259
Wait, what are you saying, Ryu-chan?

182
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:25,463
This is for the best. For your sake too.

183
00:10:26,597 --> 00:10:27,865
Mr. Miyazawa,

184
00:10:27,932 --> 00:10:30,201
shall we discuss what happens next?

185
00:10:30,801 --> 00:10:31,635
Yes.

186
00:10:32,703 --> 00:10:33,971
Wait a minute!

187
00:10:34,038 --> 00:10:36,774
I can't accept this at all! Ryu-chan!

188
00:10:36,841 --> 00:10:39,110
Kotone, calm down!

189
00:10:39,176 --> 00:10:40,277
Listen, Kotone.

190
00:10:40,344 --> 00:10:42,179
We want the best for you.

191
00:10:42,246 --> 00:10:43,981
-Let go of me!
-Wait!

192
00:10:44,048 --> 00:10:45,616
What do you even know about us?

193
00:10:45,683 --> 00:10:47,318
This is bad. Hurry!

194
00:10:47,384 --> 00:10:48,486
Calm down!

195
00:10:54,258 --> 00:10:55,126
What?

196
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:57,728
You have a problem with me?

197
00:11:03,134 --> 00:11:04,101
Kotone.

198
00:11:05,102 --> 00:11:06,904
I'm rooting for you.

199
00:11:07,671 --> 00:11:08,506
What?

200
00:11:08,572 --> 00:11:09,807
It's great, isn't it?

201
00:11:09,874 --> 00:11:13,677
A forbidden love
with a handsome man in his thirties.

202
00:11:13,744 --> 00:11:17,214
That's so cool.
You're like the heroine in a manga.

203
00:11:17,281 --> 00:11:18,883
You don't know anything…

204
00:11:20,017 --> 00:11:23,187
Can you stop treating it
like a game? It's such a pain.

205
00:11:23,821 --> 00:11:26,323
What the heck? What's with you?

206
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:27,992
Acting so high and mighty.

207
00:11:30,060 --> 00:11:31,629
Kotone.

208
00:11:32,930 --> 00:11:34,932
Tell us just one thing.

209
00:11:35,566 --> 00:11:36,400
What?

210
00:11:36,901 --> 00:11:39,870
Truth is, you two have
already done it, right?

211
00:11:39,937 --> 00:11:41,605
Shut up, you trash!

212
00:11:41,672 --> 00:11:44,208
What the hell? It was just a joke.

213
00:11:47,144 --> 00:11:48,379
Just so you all know,

214
00:11:49,413 --> 00:11:51,649
I'm not a kid like the rest of you.

215
00:11:52,683 --> 00:11:54,585
Calling each other nicknames in class,

216
00:11:54,652 --> 00:11:58,088
deciding what to do for the culture
festival… I have zero interest in that.

217
00:11:58,656 --> 00:12:00,691
So could you just leave me alone?

218
00:12:01,425 --> 00:12:02,927
Don't say that, Kotone.

219
00:12:02,993 --> 00:12:04,962
I think Onicchi can work something out.

220
00:12:05,029 --> 00:12:07,398
He's different from other adults.

221
00:12:15,372 --> 00:12:17,408
Hey, everyone to your seats.

222
00:12:24,048 --> 00:12:26,250
Mr. Onizuka, I have a question.

223
00:12:27,384 --> 00:12:30,087
What do you think
is the right thing to do?

224
00:12:30,654 --> 00:12:31,322
What?

225
00:12:31,388 --> 00:12:33,490
There's an insane number

226
00:12:33,557 --> 00:12:35,693
of teachers who end up
with students, right?

227
00:12:35,759 --> 00:12:37,328
He isn't even a teacher.

228
00:12:37,394 --> 00:12:39,396
No, but… Yeah…

229
00:12:40,164 --> 00:12:45,135
Ryunosuke is 35, and you're still 16.

230
00:12:45,202 --> 00:12:46,804
Just because of that, we can't date?

231
00:12:46,871 --> 00:12:50,274
Well, for matters like this…

232
00:12:52,743 --> 00:12:56,180
I think Ms. Kashiwabara
can explain better than me.

233
00:12:56,247 --> 00:12:58,215
Hey, don't pass it over to me again.

234
00:12:59,683 --> 00:13:01,318
Please! Help me out here.

235
00:13:01,385 --> 00:13:03,120
Do it yourself.

236
00:13:03,187 --> 00:13:05,055
-Please?
-Why me?

237
00:13:05,122 --> 00:13:06,457
Why do you always…

238
00:13:06,523 --> 00:13:07,358
Hey.

239
00:13:08,993 --> 00:13:10,995
The "Onicchi" you guys love so much

240
00:13:11,061 --> 00:13:13,397
just says the same things
as any other adult.

241
00:13:13,464 --> 00:13:15,032
No, I mean--

242
00:13:15,099 --> 00:13:19,003
Ms. Kotone, for now,
if you try to push on with your feelings,

243
00:13:19,069 --> 00:13:22,973
it will backfire, or rather,
it will cause misunderstandings.

244
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:26,577
So until you graduate high school
and become an adult,

245
00:13:26,644 --> 00:13:29,280
your only choice is to keep
your feelings for him in your heart

246
00:13:29,346 --> 00:13:31,949
and focus on your studies.

247
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:35,286
I think so too.

248
00:13:35,352 --> 00:13:36,353
So,

249
00:13:37,154 --> 00:13:38,989
for my three years of high school,

250
00:13:39,056 --> 00:13:43,460
I can't brag about the person I like
or talk to anyone about my love troubles?

251
00:13:43,527 --> 00:13:45,296
Well…

252
00:13:45,362 --> 00:13:49,833
Why do I have to hold back
on things that everyone else gets to do?

253
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:51,101
I can't accept this.

254
00:13:51,168 --> 00:13:52,670
I can't accept this at all.

255
00:13:58,242 --> 00:14:00,477
What am I supposed to do?

256
00:14:02,947 --> 00:14:04,214
I WANT TO SEE YOU

257
00:14:04,281 --> 00:14:06,016
I MISS YOU

258
00:14:06,083 --> 00:14:07,351
I'M SORRY

259
00:14:27,471 --> 00:14:28,305
Hey, Kotone.

260
00:14:29,173 --> 00:14:30,908
Want to go to karaoke or something?

261
00:14:31,475 --> 00:14:32,309
What?

262
00:14:33,043 --> 00:14:36,647
When you're frustrated,
you have to sing at the top of your lungs.

263
00:14:37,314 --> 00:14:40,851
When you rejected me, I let it all out
with the help of Onicchi and the others.

264
00:14:41,385 --> 00:14:43,287
I didn't get rejected.

265
00:14:44,121 --> 00:14:44,955
I see.

266
00:14:45,522 --> 00:14:46,557
Sorry.

267
00:14:46,623 --> 00:14:48,392
Whatever, just leave me alone.

268
00:14:51,128 --> 00:14:51,996
Hey.

269
00:14:52,696 --> 00:14:54,865
Are you sure he isn't tricking you?

270
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:57,334
No way.

271
00:14:57,401 --> 00:14:58,235
Then,

272
00:14:58,969 --> 00:15:00,671
why do you like him so much?

273
00:15:01,372 --> 00:15:04,041
Before, you said
you had no interest in romance.

274
00:15:04,108 --> 00:15:06,844
You said, when you become an adult,
you'd just use an app.

275
00:15:08,746 --> 00:15:11,448
He's someone I can respect.

276
00:15:12,683 --> 00:15:14,685
He's here from the parent company,

277
00:15:15,185 --> 00:15:19,723
so he doesn't really need to do it,
but he still repaints the peeling stairs,

278
00:15:19,790 --> 00:15:22,526
and to keep the passageways
from getting too hot,

279
00:15:22,593 --> 00:15:24,361
he sprays water on them.

280
00:15:25,362 --> 00:15:26,964
So, I asked him.

281
00:15:27,498 --> 00:15:28,999
Why are you doing this stuff?

282
00:15:31,035 --> 00:15:32,770
I just like this school.

283
00:15:33,437 --> 00:15:37,141
That man doesn't do things
to get praised by others.

284
00:15:38,142 --> 00:15:41,078
He always acts with other people's
best interests in mind.

285
00:15:41,845 --> 00:15:43,614
He's polite to everyone

286
00:15:44,815 --> 00:15:46,583
and never looks down on people.

287
00:15:47,684 --> 00:15:48,652
I see.

288
00:15:53,490 --> 00:15:56,794
What am I supposed to do?

289
00:16:01,632 --> 00:16:03,767
Say something. Hey, answer.

290
00:16:04,401 --> 00:16:05,235
What?

291
00:16:05,302 --> 00:16:06,336
Hurry it up.

292
00:16:08,038 --> 00:16:09,106
Sato.

293
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:10,774
What are you doing?

294
00:16:11,542 --> 00:16:13,544
Go home. It's nothing.

295
00:16:15,012 --> 00:16:16,080
If you say so.

296
00:16:19,483 --> 00:16:20,818
What's this?

297
00:16:20,884 --> 00:16:23,153
Aren't you popular, Soma.

298
00:16:23,854 --> 00:16:25,456
You guys go home too.

299
00:16:26,090 --> 00:16:28,892
I already told you no the other day.

300
00:16:29,393 --> 00:16:34,098
So, are you fine with that girl
being in danger?

301
00:16:34,164 --> 00:16:35,032
Hey!

302
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:37,367
Cut it out already.

303
00:16:37,434 --> 00:16:39,736
What's with that look?

304
00:16:47,044 --> 00:16:49,680
What's this? Soma, are they your friends?

305
00:16:50,547 --> 00:16:52,749
No, just classmates from middle school.

306
00:16:52,816 --> 00:16:53,784
Okay.

307
00:16:54,618 --> 00:16:58,188
I'm Eikichi Onizuka,
Soma's homeroom teacher.

308
00:17:02,292 --> 00:17:05,729
You guys, do you know much about love?

309
00:17:05,796 --> 00:17:08,432
If you do, can you give me some advice?

310
00:17:08,499 --> 00:17:12,136
Right now, one of my students
is having relationship troubles,

311
00:17:12,202 --> 00:17:13,937
and I can't think of a good answer.

312
00:17:14,004 --> 00:17:15,172
We don't care!

313
00:17:15,239 --> 00:17:17,107
What is up with you, old guy?

314
00:17:18,075 --> 00:17:19,309
Hey, Soma.

315
00:17:19,376 --> 00:17:22,312
We're heading home for today,
but think about it.

316
00:17:25,249 --> 00:17:29,586
If you're in trouble, come to me.
Okay, Soma?

317
00:17:31,188 --> 00:17:34,658
I'm actually good
at dealing with guys like them.

318
00:17:38,829 --> 00:17:40,397
I'm fine, really.

319
00:17:49,039 --> 00:17:52,376
Before we begin morning assembly,
I have an announcement to make.

320
00:17:52,943 --> 00:17:54,778
Regarding Mr. Ryunosuke Miyazawa,

321
00:17:54,845 --> 00:17:56,146
after consultation,

322
00:17:56,213 --> 00:17:58,549
we've decided to cancel
his assignment to our school

323
00:17:58,615 --> 00:18:00,984
and have him return to the parent company.

324
00:18:01,618 --> 00:18:03,654
Wait a minute, Vice Principal.

325
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,122
What is it, Mr. Onizuka?

326
00:18:05,189 --> 00:18:07,658
Ryunosuke didn't do anything wrong.

327
00:18:07,724 --> 00:18:09,359
Is it really okay to end things like this?

328
00:18:09,927 --> 00:18:12,696
Aren't you just making him a scapegoat?

329
00:18:12,763 --> 00:18:15,499
Then do you have
a better solution, Mr. Onizuka?

330
00:18:15,566 --> 00:18:16,833
Well…

331
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,001
It's fine, Mr. Onizuka.

332
00:18:18,068 --> 00:18:19,036
But…

333
00:18:19,102 --> 00:18:21,672
I was careless. It's my fault.

334
00:18:28,245 --> 00:18:29,079
All right…

335
00:18:29,913 --> 00:18:30,881
Everyone,

336
00:18:31,415 --> 00:18:35,452
I am truly sorry
for causing you all so much trouble.

337
00:18:38,922 --> 00:18:41,391
I may not have the right to say this,

338
00:18:42,226 --> 00:18:44,728
but please, do all you can

339
00:18:45,762 --> 00:18:51,168
so every student at this school
can graduate with a smile on their face.

340
00:18:52,536 --> 00:18:53,704
Please.

341
00:18:59,843 --> 00:19:01,111
Mr. Miyazawa.

342
00:19:01,878 --> 00:19:02,779
Yes?

343
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:05,482
Thank you for everything.

344
00:19:07,150 --> 00:19:10,721
For watering the plants,
painting the walls,

345
00:19:10,787 --> 00:19:11,989
and everything else…

346
00:19:15,759 --> 00:19:16,593
It's nothing.

347
00:19:20,297 --> 00:19:21,465
Ryu-chan!

348
00:19:24,768 --> 00:19:26,336
Are you really fine with this?

349
00:19:26,403 --> 00:19:28,839
We really can't see each other again?

350
00:19:30,874 --> 00:19:33,577
I told you. This is the best choice.

351
00:19:33,644 --> 00:19:34,645
Then…

352
00:19:35,245 --> 00:19:37,848
Will you forget all
the fun times we had together too?

353
00:19:38,548 --> 00:19:41,218
When I called you to say,
"The moon is full tonight,"

354
00:19:41,285 --> 00:19:44,288
you taught me so many things
while looking at the same moon.

355
00:19:44,354 --> 00:19:46,923
Like how Soseki Natsume
translated "I love you"

356
00:19:46,990 --> 00:19:49,993
as "The moon is beautiful, isn't it?"

357
00:19:50,060 --> 00:19:51,295
I…

358
00:19:52,896 --> 00:19:56,199
When I'm with you, Ryu-chan,
I'm filled with gentle feelings.

359
00:19:57,401 --> 00:19:59,736
I feel like I have to be a good person.

360
00:20:00,270 --> 00:20:02,272
What am I supposed to do
with these feelings

361
00:20:02,339 --> 00:20:03,840
from now on?

362
00:20:03,907 --> 00:20:04,875
I have no other choice!

363
00:20:06,476 --> 00:20:08,712
It's causing trouble for so many people.

364
00:20:08,779 --> 00:20:11,315
Like your parents, or Mr. Onizuka…

365
00:20:12,182 --> 00:20:13,583
What about me?

366
00:20:15,018 --> 00:20:17,120
My feelings don't matter?

367
00:20:19,089 --> 00:20:20,223
Well…

368
00:20:24,227 --> 00:20:25,062
I'm sorry.

369
00:20:34,538 --> 00:20:37,507
Kotone, homeroom has already started.

370
00:20:40,377 --> 00:20:41,745
What are you doing, Kotone?

371
00:20:42,379 --> 00:20:44,114
I'm quitting high school.

372
00:20:44,181 --> 00:20:45,015
What?

373
00:20:45,082 --> 00:20:46,083
That way,

374
00:20:46,817 --> 00:20:48,318
I'll be free to date Ryu-chan.

375
00:20:49,419 --> 00:20:51,221
What are you talking about, Kotone?

376
00:20:51,288 --> 00:20:54,925
That's right. What about university?
You have excellent grades.

377
00:20:55,559 --> 00:20:57,694
Don't you have dreams for the future?

378
00:20:57,761 --> 00:21:00,697
There are things
you want to study at university, right?

379
00:21:01,998 --> 00:21:03,100
I just…

380
00:21:04,067 --> 00:21:05,936
love him, that's all.

381
00:21:06,603 --> 00:21:07,504
And yet…

382
00:21:08,638 --> 00:21:10,974
Why do people have to look
at me like I'm weird?

383
00:21:11,775 --> 00:21:16,646
I just want to spend time with him,
like any normal couple would.

384
00:21:17,948 --> 00:21:19,549
What's so wrong with that?

385
00:21:19,616 --> 00:21:21,952
Kotone, I understand how you feel, but…

386
00:21:22,018 --> 00:21:22,886
No.

387
00:21:23,787 --> 00:21:24,988
Nobody understands.

388
00:21:25,489 --> 00:21:26,823
That's why, from now on,

389
00:21:27,457 --> 00:21:28,759
whatever people say,

390
00:21:28,825 --> 00:21:31,995
I will trust only myself
and live by reading the books I like.

391
00:21:35,399 --> 00:21:38,802
That will be way more educational
than anything taught here, anyway.

392
00:21:49,146 --> 00:21:51,314
DEAR AZUSA

393
00:21:51,381 --> 00:21:56,286
IF IT WERE YOU,
WHAT WOULD YOU SAY TO KOTONE?

394
00:22:06,263 --> 00:22:07,864
Are you not going home yet?

395
00:22:08,999 --> 00:22:09,933
Yes.

396
00:22:10,901 --> 00:22:12,068
It's like…

397
00:22:12,602 --> 00:22:16,540
I just don't know what to do anymore.

398
00:22:21,812 --> 00:22:22,779
Mr. Onizuka.

399
00:22:28,718 --> 00:22:30,754
Yes? Murai?

400
00:22:31,488 --> 00:22:32,456
What's up?

401
00:22:32,956 --> 00:22:34,958
FUSION CUISINE

402
00:22:35,025 --> 00:22:36,793
Where's Masaru?

403
00:22:39,429 --> 00:22:40,497
What?

404
00:22:42,365 --> 00:22:43,433
Hey.

405
00:22:43,934 --> 00:22:45,802
Masaru, what the hell are you doing?

406
00:22:46,470 --> 00:22:47,537
Onicchi,

407
00:22:48,171 --> 00:22:49,306
what should I do?

408
00:22:49,806 --> 00:22:50,974
Kotone…

409
00:22:51,041 --> 00:22:51,875
What?

410
00:22:51,942 --> 00:22:53,009
Kotone…

411
00:22:53,076 --> 00:22:55,212
Did something happen with her?

412
00:22:56,313 --> 00:22:59,850
When I heard from my wife
that she said she was quitting school,

413
00:22:59,916 --> 00:23:02,519
I told her not to be ridiculous
and grabbed her hair.

414
00:23:03,086 --> 00:23:04,421
And then she said,

415
00:23:04,488 --> 00:23:07,257
"I don't think of you as my father
anymore," and stormed out.

416
00:23:07,324 --> 00:23:09,359
What? Are you serious?

417
00:23:10,060 --> 00:23:11,261
What should I do, Onicchi?

418
00:23:11,328 --> 00:23:13,964
We have to look for her! Let's go!

419
00:23:14,030 --> 00:23:17,067
I can't, I'm drunk.

420
00:23:17,133 --> 00:23:18,835
Don't sound so pathetic!

421
00:23:18,902 --> 00:23:21,805
Onicchi! Why didn't you
keep an eye on her?

422
00:23:21,872 --> 00:23:22,706
Shut up!

423
00:23:22,772 --> 00:23:25,475
You let that bastard
get close to my daughter!

424
00:23:25,542 --> 00:23:27,978
You idiot, Ryunosuke
isn't that kind of guy!

425
00:23:28,044 --> 00:23:30,747
Yeah, Masaru. What's the problem, anyway?

426
00:23:30,814 --> 00:23:33,583
If they truly love each other,
does their age really matter?

427
00:23:33,650 --> 00:23:37,153
You're not married, so you don't
understand how a parent feels.

428
00:23:38,288 --> 00:23:39,155
But…

429
00:23:39,689 --> 00:23:43,226
I can understand what it's like to
single-mindedly love someone, though.

430
00:23:43,793 --> 00:23:45,161
What do you mean, Murai?

431
00:23:46,496 --> 00:23:49,132
This guy still has feelings for Miyabi.

432
00:23:51,835 --> 00:23:52,969
Ever since high school?

433
00:23:53,670 --> 00:23:54,671
All this time?

434
00:23:55,472 --> 00:23:56,439
Shut up.

435
00:23:56,973 --> 00:23:59,309
You're the same.
You've only ever loved Ms. Fuyutsuki.

436
00:23:59,376 --> 00:24:01,578
You were a virgin until you got married.

437
00:24:01,645 --> 00:24:04,648
So you've only ever dated one woman.

438
00:24:04,714 --> 00:24:06,416
What, is that so?

439
00:24:06,483 --> 00:24:08,585
We're not talking about me.

440
00:24:08,652 --> 00:24:10,420
I've been curious for a while.

441
00:24:10,487 --> 00:24:13,657
A beautiful teacher like you,
do you have someone you like?

442
00:24:13,723 --> 00:24:16,192
What? I don't have anyone right now…

443
00:24:16,259 --> 00:24:17,961
Then how about Onicchi?

444
00:24:18,028 --> 00:24:20,096
His wife is leaving him anyway.

445
00:24:20,163 --> 00:24:21,031
What?

446
00:24:22,165 --> 00:24:24,167
You're not making any sense, man.

447
00:24:24,234 --> 00:24:26,469
Hey, we have to go look for Kotone!

448
00:24:26,536 --> 00:24:28,572
Hey, wake up!

449
00:24:28,638 --> 00:24:31,041
No way, I'm drunk!

450
00:24:34,878 --> 00:24:35,745
Ryunosuke.

451
00:24:35,812 --> 00:24:37,013
Sorry for the wait.

452
00:24:37,881 --> 00:24:40,784
I wrote down a list
of places she might go.

453
00:24:40,850 --> 00:24:41,685
Okay.

454
00:24:43,987 --> 00:24:45,021
Ryunosuke.

455
00:24:45,689 --> 00:24:46,690
What is it?

456
00:24:48,091 --> 00:24:50,827
What do you really want to do?

457
00:24:51,561 --> 00:24:52,262
What?

458
00:24:53,730 --> 00:24:57,100
You're acting all mature, saying you
stepped back for Kotone's sake,

459
00:24:57,167 --> 00:24:58,902
but what are your true feelings?

460
00:24:58,969 --> 00:25:00,637
Are you fine with leaving her?

461
00:25:01,338 --> 00:25:02,939
There's no other choice…

462
00:25:03,006 --> 00:25:05,075
This is what's best for her.

463
00:25:06,309 --> 00:25:09,446
Kotone doesn't look happy
right now, though.

464
00:25:10,614 --> 00:25:11,314
What?

465
00:25:12,582 --> 00:25:14,551
It's fine to play the good guy,

466
00:25:14,618 --> 00:25:18,221
but the problem here is you never told
Kotone your true feelings.

467
00:25:19,823 --> 00:25:21,691
What's the point?

468
00:25:21,758 --> 00:25:23,860
I've decided
we won't see each other again.

469
00:25:25,662 --> 00:25:29,766
Back in high school,
you barely came to school

470
00:25:29,833 --> 00:25:33,570
and were a wild kid who smoked and drank.

471
00:25:34,170 --> 00:25:37,641
Now look what a sensible adult
you have become.

472
00:25:42,379 --> 00:25:43,847
What's with that look?

473
00:25:44,381 --> 00:25:45,715
Say what you want to say.

474
00:25:47,550 --> 00:25:49,419
You have no right
to act all high and mighty.

475
00:25:50,186 --> 00:25:53,356
I thought you would do
something more to help,

476
00:25:53,423 --> 00:25:57,727
but you just made excuses, saying you're
bad at romance, and didn't help at all.

477
00:25:58,461 --> 00:26:01,631
A guy like you wouldn't understand
how hard it is to be a teacher!

478
00:26:01,698 --> 00:26:04,134
Don't act cocky
just because you're a teacher!

479
00:26:04,200 --> 00:26:06,503
You're still doing as you please…

480
00:26:06,569 --> 00:26:08,605
When will you become a real teacher?

481
00:26:08,672 --> 00:26:12,275
This is why your wife is leaving you!

482
00:26:12,342 --> 00:26:13,843
What did you say?

483
00:26:13,910 --> 00:26:16,446
What? If you have a complaint,
let me hear it!

484
00:26:16,513 --> 00:26:20,417
Can you really proudly call yourself
a Great Teacher?

485
00:26:21,217 --> 00:26:21,885
What?

486
00:26:21,951 --> 00:26:24,688
Can you say from the bottom of your heart,

487
00:26:24,754 --> 00:26:27,824
"The students of Seishin
absolutely need me"?

488
00:26:28,391 --> 00:26:30,093
Well, can you?

489
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:31,294
You bastard,

490
00:26:31,361 --> 00:26:33,963
picking on the thing
I'm most sensitive about…

491
00:26:34,030 --> 00:26:35,699
Hit me if you want to.

492
00:26:35,765 --> 00:26:39,302
I used to get beaten up
all the time, so I'm used to it.

493
00:26:47,410 --> 00:26:48,578
I already decided

494
00:26:49,646 --> 00:26:51,848
that I'm not going to hit anyone anymore.

495
00:26:56,453 --> 00:26:57,687
So,

496
00:26:58,855 --> 00:27:00,323
I'm going to do this instead!

497
00:27:07,063 --> 00:27:08,665
What are you doing?

498
00:27:08,732 --> 00:27:10,600
I didn't hit you!

499
00:27:11,334 --> 00:27:12,736
What the heck?

500
00:27:12,802 --> 00:27:15,605
Are you a baseball manager
arguing with the umpire?

501
00:27:15,672 --> 00:27:18,775
I have to do this, or I'll remain mad!
After everything you said!

502
00:27:18,842 --> 00:27:19,776
Shut up!

503
00:27:19,843 --> 00:27:22,412
I've also held back this whole time!

504
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:25,081
You bastard!

505
00:27:26,216 --> 00:27:27,617
Take this, bastard!

506
00:27:27,684 --> 00:27:30,186
-Don't think you can just…
-Wait, a phone call.

507
00:27:31,588 --> 00:27:32,522
Wait.

508
00:27:34,491 --> 00:27:35,759
It's Ms. Kashiwabara.

509
00:27:36,392 --> 00:27:37,660
Hello?

510
00:27:38,628 --> 00:27:41,197
Okay. I'll be right there.

511
00:27:44,067 --> 00:27:46,536
They found Kotone.

512
00:27:49,739 --> 00:27:51,141
You're not going?

513
00:27:53,743 --> 00:27:56,479
I promised that I wouldn't
see her anymore.

514
00:27:57,747 --> 00:27:59,816
There you go again…

515
00:28:04,354 --> 00:28:06,356
Please, Mr. Onizuka.

516
00:28:08,158 --> 00:28:11,528
Please try to persuade Kotone,

517
00:28:12,128 --> 00:28:14,631
so she won't try to quit school!

518
00:28:17,066 --> 00:28:20,336
She is more sensitive than anyone else

519
00:28:21,404 --> 00:28:23,072
and has infinite potential.

520
00:28:24,641 --> 00:28:25,809
But…

521
00:28:27,443 --> 00:28:31,047
she's stubborn and doesn't know
how to rely on others.

522
00:28:31,681 --> 00:28:34,250
That's what worries me.

523
00:28:36,486 --> 00:28:37,487
So…

524
00:28:40,924 --> 00:28:43,092
As she's about to lose hope,

525
00:28:45,228 --> 00:28:49,666
please do what you can
to guide her back to the right path.

526
00:28:52,235 --> 00:28:55,238
Just like you did for me, back then.

527
00:29:11,921 --> 00:29:12,956
Kotone?

528
00:29:16,159 --> 00:29:18,161
How did you find her?

529
00:29:18,228 --> 00:29:21,064
I searched every single net cafe
around this area.

530
00:29:22,732 --> 00:29:23,600
I see.

531
00:29:23,666 --> 00:29:25,268
She says she's never going home.

532
00:29:25,335 --> 00:29:27,971
She'll quit school, work part-time…

533
00:29:28,037 --> 00:29:30,340
For now, I'm letting her stay at my place.

534
00:29:35,445 --> 00:29:38,514
RESUME - KOTONE WAKATSUKI
SEISHIN ACADEMY

535
00:29:40,016 --> 00:29:42,018
DROPPED OUT

536
00:29:51,995 --> 00:29:53,696
What are you doing, Kotone?

537
00:29:54,264 --> 00:29:57,166
Just so you know,
I will not change my mind.

538
00:30:00,403 --> 00:30:01,971
Cut it out already.

539
00:30:03,273 --> 00:30:07,443
Ryunosuke doesn't want this either.

540
00:30:10,146 --> 00:30:12,448
He went through hard times because of me.

541
00:30:13,049 --> 00:30:15,451
I can't just go to school
like nothing happened.

542
00:30:20,924 --> 00:30:22,158
Hey, Kotone.

543
00:30:22,225 --> 00:30:23,259
What is it?

544
00:30:25,595 --> 00:30:28,264
I am a teacher.

545
00:30:29,832 --> 00:30:31,968
What? I know, why bring it up…

546
00:30:32,035 --> 00:30:32,902
No, so…

547
00:30:33,436 --> 00:30:37,540
today I will talk to you as a teacher.

548
00:30:38,942 --> 00:30:42,745
I won't pass the ball to Ms. Kashiwabara
and ask for help anymore.

549
00:30:43,413 --> 00:30:47,216
If I keep doing that, I won't be able
to become a real teacher.

550
00:30:47,283 --> 00:30:49,152
-Mr. Onizuka.
-Ms. Kashiwabara.

551
00:30:49,218 --> 00:30:52,322
Just watch, don't say anything, okay?

552
00:30:52,889 --> 00:30:53,957
I understand.

553
00:31:05,501 --> 00:31:06,569
Hey, Kotone.

554
00:31:10,606 --> 00:31:13,676
You want to be with Ryunosuke

555
00:31:14,410 --> 00:31:16,813
for the rest of your life, I get that.

556
00:31:17,914 --> 00:31:19,382
But right now,

557
00:31:19,449 --> 00:31:22,018
I don't think
you have the right to date him.

558
00:31:22,919 --> 00:31:24,220
Because I'm a minor?

559
00:31:24,287 --> 00:31:26,589
No, because…

560
00:31:28,291 --> 00:31:32,261
It's like no matter how much
I insist I'm a good teacher,

561
00:31:32,328 --> 00:31:34,731
the people around me won't acknowledge it.

562
00:31:35,565 --> 00:31:39,068
No matter how purely you love Ryunosuke…

563
00:31:39,635 --> 00:31:42,138
The people around you
won't acknowledge it.

564
00:31:43,339 --> 00:31:46,609
They'll just say
you're still young and naive.

565
00:31:47,577 --> 00:31:48,578
That's right, so…

566
00:31:48,644 --> 00:31:51,214
Miss, can you please stay quiet?

567
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:52,515
Sorry, couldn't help it.

568
00:31:53,383 --> 00:31:54,784
Then what should I do?

569
00:31:56,686 --> 00:31:59,255
You have to prove it to them.

570
00:32:01,124 --> 00:32:05,028
That you can keep these feelings
until you graduate high school.

571
00:32:05,094 --> 00:32:07,864
Why do I have to care
about what others think?

572
00:32:07,930 --> 00:32:09,465
That's…

573
00:32:10,400 --> 00:32:11,300
Oh, right.

574
00:32:15,238 --> 00:32:17,273
Because…

575
00:32:22,845 --> 00:32:24,347
No human being

576
00:32:26,182 --> 00:32:28,117
can go through life

577
00:32:29,352 --> 00:32:30,520
without relying on others.

578
00:32:30,586 --> 00:32:32,822
There are people who live on
deserted islands, though.

579
00:32:34,457 --> 00:32:35,792
That's true.

580
00:32:36,392 --> 00:32:37,326
But…

581
00:32:38,895 --> 00:32:41,697
living on a deserted island gets lonely.

582
00:32:43,332 --> 00:32:47,270
I don't want you to live
a lonely life from here on out.

583
00:32:48,337 --> 00:32:53,409
High school is a wonderful time,
so you have to enjoy your youth and laugh.

584
00:32:54,343 --> 00:32:56,379
You have to be full of hope.

585
00:32:57,680 --> 00:33:01,317
And yet Ryunosuke made you sad!
That guy is no good!

586
00:33:01,384 --> 00:33:04,187
Ryunosuke understands that too.

587
00:33:05,154 --> 00:33:08,524
That's why he knows
you have to be apart for now.

588
00:33:13,396 --> 00:33:14,497
Kotone,

589
00:33:16,199 --> 00:33:17,767
if you love him,

590
00:33:19,535 --> 00:33:21,104
after you graduate high school…

591
00:33:25,108 --> 00:33:28,544
Date him freely, once you turn 18.

592
00:33:28,611 --> 00:33:31,948
But his feelings might change before then.

593
00:33:34,283 --> 00:33:35,485
Maybe.

594
00:33:36,085 --> 00:33:37,420
That is a possibility.

595
00:33:39,122 --> 00:33:42,992
But I still believe
that both of your feelings won't change.

596
00:33:43,693 --> 00:33:47,396
Because both you and Ryunosuke
are students I'm proud of,

597
00:33:47,463 --> 00:33:52,435
and I know you are pure-hearted,
kind human beings.

598
00:33:52,502 --> 00:33:53,870
So I…

599
00:33:55,171 --> 00:33:58,007
I won't believe in a future
where you two can't be together.

600
00:33:58,975 --> 00:34:01,844
I believe in a future where you both
are smiling happily together.

601
00:34:01,911 --> 00:34:05,214
No matter what anyone says,
I believe it. I want to!

602
00:34:05,781 --> 00:34:07,150
Let me believe in it.

603
00:34:12,622 --> 00:34:14,423
Mr. Onizuka.

604
00:34:16,526 --> 00:34:17,360
Yes?

605
00:34:19,295 --> 00:34:21,197
Can I speak too?

606
00:34:24,033 --> 00:34:25,168
Go ahead.

607
00:34:25,234 --> 00:34:28,037
I have said all I had to say.

608
00:34:34,143 --> 00:34:35,111
Kotone,

609
00:34:36,612 --> 00:34:40,149
I also believe in the future
Mr. Onizuka talked about.

610
00:34:41,417 --> 00:34:44,186
Let's work hard to make it come true.

611
00:34:45,555 --> 00:34:48,691
You said all you need are books,

612
00:34:49,458 --> 00:34:52,328
but when you're in trouble,
what supports you in the end

613
00:34:52,395 --> 00:34:53,596
aren't books,

614
00:34:54,597 --> 00:34:58,501
but the words of the people you've met
and the time you spent with them.

615
00:35:00,336 --> 00:35:01,604
I really hope

616
00:35:02,638 --> 00:35:04,907
you won't forget
what Mr. Onizuka just said.

617
00:35:06,442 --> 00:35:08,211
Remember it for the rest of your life.

618
00:35:24,727 --> 00:35:26,362
What a hassle.

619
00:35:27,029 --> 00:35:29,765
I want to become an adult quickly.

620
00:35:31,567 --> 00:35:33,569
But it's not like I have a time machine,

621
00:35:34,937 --> 00:35:38,274
so I guess I'll go to school and graduate.

622
00:35:41,944 --> 00:35:43,045
Really?

623
00:35:48,184 --> 00:35:49,151
Really?

624
00:35:53,623 --> 00:35:55,891
I'm so ridiculously happy!

625
00:35:56,926 --> 00:35:58,261
You don't have to be that happy.

626
00:35:58,327 --> 00:35:59,328
No, but…

627
00:35:59,862 --> 00:36:00,997
This is the first time

628
00:36:02,565 --> 00:36:05,501
I've lectured someone
like a real teacher and succeeded!

629
00:36:09,005 --> 00:36:09,972
You are

630
00:36:10,940 --> 00:36:13,843
my very first real student.
It's worth commemorating.

631
00:36:15,311 --> 00:36:17,847
I'll never forget this day
for the rest of my life.

632
00:36:20,182 --> 00:36:21,217
What's with you?

633
00:36:47,743 --> 00:36:48,778
Hello.

634
00:36:50,046 --> 00:36:51,347
What are you doing?

635
00:36:53,783 --> 00:36:55,117
I was looking at the moon.

636
00:36:58,688 --> 00:37:00,189
Ryu-chan, I decided

637
00:37:02,558 --> 00:37:04,293
to trust Onicchi.

638
00:37:06,128 --> 00:37:07,096
I see.

639
00:37:08,931 --> 00:37:11,834
It will be okay, right?

640
00:37:13,035 --> 00:37:16,372
That man is the best teacher
I've ever had, you know.

641
00:37:18,507 --> 00:37:19,608
I'm sorry.

642
00:37:20,409 --> 00:37:22,445
For causing you so many painful feelings.

643
00:37:23,079 --> 00:37:24,747
Enough of that already.

644
00:37:25,681 --> 00:37:27,817
Tell me how you feel, Ryu-chan.

645
00:37:29,118 --> 00:37:29,952
What?

646
00:37:30,586 --> 00:37:33,055
I still haven't heard
what you think of me.

647
00:37:36,092 --> 00:37:37,426
Kotone.

648
00:37:38,994 --> 00:37:39,862
Yes?

649
00:37:41,330 --> 00:37:44,200
The moon is beautiful, isn't it?

650
00:37:46,469 --> 00:37:47,670
Ryunosuke.

651
00:37:49,939 --> 00:37:50,840
Yes.

652
00:37:52,908 --> 00:37:54,543
The moon is beautiful, isn't it?

653
00:38:04,420 --> 00:38:05,988
Thank you, Onicchi.

654
00:38:06,055 --> 00:38:07,423
For what?

655
00:38:08,157 --> 00:38:12,695
Yesterday, Kotone came back home
and said she's going to school as usual.

656
00:38:12,762 --> 00:38:14,163
And…

657
00:38:14,230 --> 00:38:16,298
Ryunosuke came to apologize too.

658
00:38:17,032 --> 00:38:20,603
He said once Kotone graduates,
he'll date her for real.

659
00:38:21,871 --> 00:38:22,872
I see.

660
00:38:23,873 --> 00:38:25,808
For now, I'm relieved.

661
00:38:25,875 --> 00:38:29,912
When it comes to my daughter,
I kind of lack confidence.

662
00:38:29,979 --> 00:38:31,714
I didn't know how to interact with her.

663
00:38:34,250 --> 00:38:35,351
It's okay.

664
00:38:35,918 --> 00:38:39,555
Your daughter knows very well
that you love her a lot.

665
00:38:39,622 --> 00:38:41,257
You think so, Mr. Onizuka?

666
00:38:44,326 --> 00:38:45,594
-You know, today…
-What?

667
00:38:45,661 --> 00:38:47,396
You feel like a real teacher.

668
00:38:47,463 --> 00:38:49,098
Well, you know,

669
00:38:49,865 --> 00:38:53,002
I've become a different man. I guess.

670
00:38:54,236 --> 00:38:56,605
CLASS 1-B

671
00:39:00,342 --> 00:39:01,343
Hey, everyone.

672
00:39:01,410 --> 00:39:04,713
If we don't decide soon,
we won't be able to prepare in time.

673
00:39:04,780 --> 00:39:07,416
Hey, does anyone have an idea?

674
00:39:08,250 --> 00:39:11,120
If we can't decide on anything,
should we just give up?

675
00:39:11,187 --> 00:39:12,621
We can't do that.

676
00:39:15,524 --> 00:39:18,694
Because I've decided to enjoy
my youth with all of you.

677
00:39:19,295 --> 00:39:23,699
From now on, I want to talk with everyone,
make lots of good memories, and graduate.

678
00:39:24,266 --> 00:39:27,770
So doing nothing for the culture festival
is out of the question!

679
00:39:30,739 --> 00:39:32,608
No need to get so worked up.

680
00:39:33,342 --> 00:39:34,243
Sorry.

681
00:39:35,511 --> 00:39:36,812
But I want to

682
00:39:38,414 --> 00:39:40,149
become friends with you all.

683
00:39:41,617 --> 00:39:45,554
Up until now, I only read books
and put out a "don't bother me" vibe,

684
00:39:46,222 --> 00:39:49,992
but I'll stop doing that
and talk about my love troubles too.

685
00:39:50,593 --> 00:39:51,660
So…

686
00:39:55,498 --> 00:39:58,400
We have to decide on a nickname then.

687
00:39:58,901 --> 00:40:01,003
-What?
-But what should it be?

688
00:40:01,837 --> 00:40:04,473
How about Koto-koto,
or Love-Love Princess?

689
00:40:04,540 --> 00:40:07,076
You don't need to speak up
at times like this.

690
00:40:07,142 --> 00:40:09,144
How about Single-Minded? Or Baby Face?

691
00:40:09,211 --> 00:40:10,946
Baby Face is nice.

692
00:40:11,013 --> 00:40:12,081
Well then.

693
00:40:12,748 --> 00:40:15,084
How about Miss Youth?

694
00:40:15,150 --> 00:40:16,151
That's so lame!

695
00:40:16,952 --> 00:40:20,356
"Miss Youth" is a bit much…

696
00:40:21,090 --> 00:40:23,626
Got it! How about just MY?

697
00:40:24,527 --> 00:40:25,694
Nice!

698
00:40:25,761 --> 00:40:27,596
Nice to meet you, MY!

699
00:40:28,397 --> 00:40:29,965
Thank you, everyone.

700
00:40:36,038 --> 00:40:38,474
So, what are we doing
for the culture festival?

701
00:40:48,951 --> 00:40:49,885
Hey, Yuu.

702
00:40:49,952 --> 00:40:51,220
What is it?

703
00:40:52,054 --> 00:40:54,890
I've been waiting
this whole time, you know.

704
00:40:55,891 --> 00:41:01,864
You should suggest that
the whole class do drills with you.

705
00:41:01,931 --> 00:41:04,466
I wanted to do that too,

706
00:41:05,668 --> 00:41:07,503
but I just lacked the courage…

707
00:41:07,570 --> 00:41:08,671
Then,

708
00:41:09,405 --> 00:41:13,042
let's teach the whole school
how wonderful a drill team can be!

709
00:41:18,647 --> 00:41:20,015
How about it, everyone?

710
00:41:20,082 --> 00:41:24,753
I think drills let us express the joy
of connecting with the people around you.

711
00:41:25,321 --> 00:41:29,858
Don't you think it'd be amazing
if we could do that as a whole class?

712
00:41:30,526 --> 00:41:31,660
That's right, everyone!

713
00:41:31,727 --> 00:41:33,395
Let's do it!

714
00:41:33,996 --> 00:41:34,897
Let's do it.

715
00:41:34,964 --> 00:41:35,798
Shall we?

716
00:41:35,864 --> 00:41:36,732
Yes.

717
00:41:36,799 --> 00:41:37,967
Let's do it!

718
00:41:38,033 --> 00:41:39,768
-I'm in!
-Yeah!

719
00:41:39,835 --> 00:41:41,403
-Us too!
-Yes!

720
00:41:41,470 --> 00:41:43,038
I'm still club president, okay?

721
00:41:43,105 --> 00:41:43,939
I know!

722
00:41:45,140 --> 00:41:46,575
All right then,

723
00:41:46,642 --> 00:41:49,411
let's do our best
for the culture festival!

724
00:41:50,312 --> 00:41:53,082
Yeah!

725
00:42:09,565 --> 00:42:12,534
Touch, touch, friends!

726
00:42:12,601 --> 00:42:14,970
Touch, touch, friends!

727
00:42:21,243 --> 00:42:22,745
Why don't you join in too?

728
00:42:23,879 --> 00:42:25,214
I'm good.

729
00:42:26,048 --> 00:42:26,915
Fine.

730
00:42:42,798 --> 00:42:43,699
Thank goodness.

731
00:42:43,766 --> 00:42:46,201
We finally decided
what to do for the festival.

732
00:42:48,137 --> 00:42:49,438
Is something wrong?

733
00:42:52,608 --> 00:42:53,575
Ms. Kashiwabara.

734
00:42:54,276 --> 00:42:55,144
Yes?

735
00:42:56,345 --> 00:42:58,380
I have something important
to discuss with you.

736
00:42:59,548 --> 00:43:01,050
Really? What is it?

737
00:43:07,222 --> 00:43:10,659
Wait a minute. I feel like something
like this happened before.

738
00:43:12,127 --> 00:43:15,197
But we're strictly colleagues, so…

739
00:43:16,131 --> 00:43:18,000
Are you misunderstanding something?

740
00:43:21,670 --> 00:43:22,604
Then, what is it?

741
00:43:23,305 --> 00:43:24,273
Actually,

742
00:43:25,040 --> 00:43:27,476
I got a text from my wife.

743
00:43:28,444 --> 00:43:34,183
TIME'S UP. SINCE IT SEEMS YOU CAN'T
ANSWER WHAT A "GREAT TEACHER" IS,

744
00:43:34,249 --> 00:43:38,087
PLEASE SIGN THE DIVORCE PAPERS

745
00:43:39,321 --> 00:43:42,558
Just when I finally gained
a little confidence as a teacher…

746
00:43:43,225 --> 00:43:44,993
What am I supposed to do now?

747
00:43:45,060 --> 00:43:46,595
Well, that's…

748
00:43:52,434 --> 00:43:53,802
Class is starting.

749
00:44:08,751 --> 00:44:11,420
Open your textbooks…

750
00:44:12,621 --> 00:44:13,288
Soma Sato!

751
00:44:13,355 --> 00:44:15,090
Is Soma Sato here?

752
00:44:17,860 --> 00:44:20,462
Hey! What on earth have you done?

753
00:44:20,529 --> 00:44:22,798
What's wrong, Vice Principal?

754
00:44:22,865 --> 00:44:24,299
The police are here!

755
00:44:24,800 --> 00:44:26,001
To arrest him, they say!

756
00:44:27,035 --> 00:44:28,036
What?

757
00:44:35,677 --> 00:44:37,146
A teacher, committing assault?

758
00:44:37,212 --> 00:44:40,582
This time you are getting fired for sure!

759
00:44:40,649 --> 00:44:42,684
Should you really be doing this?

760
00:44:42,751 --> 00:44:45,120
Could you let him teach one last lesson?

761
00:44:45,187 --> 00:44:47,890
He doesn't want to leave us all alone.

762
00:44:47,956 --> 00:44:50,793
"Your youth is precious, don't waste it!"

763
00:44:50,859 --> 00:44:53,228
He can voluntarily drop out
before the decision is made.

764
00:44:53,295 --> 00:44:54,530
I've decided to quit.

765
00:44:55,564 --> 00:44:57,366
Shut up for a bit!

766
00:44:57,432 --> 00:45:00,135
Onicchi!

767
00:45:00,202 --> 00:45:03,138
You are all great!

768
00:45:03,205 --> 00:45:04,173
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

